Deferred. The body is free markdown and stays that way until the trigger.

Every ticket in this tracker ends with a "Done when ..." paragraph, which is
already a convention — an unenforced one that nothing reads. The question is
whether that deserves structure: a field, a fenced block, a heading check
looks for.

Against: the body is the one place with no rules, which is why writing
findings into it needs no bookkeeping. A checked-for heading is a schema for
prose, and prose that must satisfy a checker gets written for the checker.

Trigger: agents guessing wrong about when a ticket is done. That is
observable — a ticket closed with work left, or left open with none.

If it ever happens, the cheapest version is a convention the reference
states and check does not enforce, which is what "Done when" already is.
